---
// The /events page's title and standfirst, and nothing else — no band, no
// padding of its own.
//
// Split out of EventsPage so the route can render it ABOVE the Luma calendar.
// It used to sit below, which meant the page opened on the embed's own heading
// ("Full events calendar") and a visitor's first line of text was Luma's rather
// than the site's — a page that does not say what it is until you have scrolled
// past a third-party frame.
//
// Deliberately NOT a section: each caller puts it inside its own `.s-section` /
// `.s-inner`, so it sits on the site's shared band rhythm rather than inventing
// a second one beside it. EventsPage still renders it by default, which is what
// keeps the isolated-component scenarios of the events body unchanged; the
// route passes `showIntro={false}` because it places this itself, higher up.
---

<h1 class="s-title">Events</h1>
<p class="events-lede">
  In-person events, panels, and gatherings across our Boston &amp; Cambridge, New
  York, London, DC &amp; DMV, and Seattle chapters, plus a global community
  connected online.
</p>

<style>
  .events-lede {
    color: var(--color-muted);
    max-width: var(--text-width);
    margin: 0 auto var(--space-lg);
  }
</style>
